WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:14,620
Spending one day at my sister-in-law's who smokes at her house caused my cancer to get worse.

00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:28,540
Normally I'd say no, but the truth is that anything that can just really, you know, smoking

00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:36,500
has benzines in the smoke, it has all sorts of other negative things in the smoke.

00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:44,340
Very high oxidation rate of cigarette smoke, if you're dealing with detoxification pathways

00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:50,420
already, could it cause a flare-up because it's going to cause inflammation possibly,

00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:56,620
especially if you have antibodies to benzine, which isn't that uncommon.

00:00:56,620 --> 00:01:05,900
So you could look at what's called a Syrex Array 5, and that will give you that will show

00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:10,900
that's an antibody test. It will show if you have antibodies to cigarette smoke.

00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:18,900
I can't wait till they add antibodies to mRNA viruses into that test, hopefully.

00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:24,900
Maybe they never will just for a medical legal reasons, but I do know that we've had people that

00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:31,900
went and visited people that were vaccinated, and their cancer got worse noticeably

00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:35,900
because they had a visible lymphoma, and it got worse.

00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:40,900
We've had lots of people that got vaccinated, and their cancer was in remission, and their cancer

00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:43,900
just took off, and they passed away.

00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:52,900
So I do know that exposure to chemicals and exposure to things that cause inflammatory processes

00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:57,900
and cell damage and oxidation can cause a cancer to grow.

00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:02,900
Years ago, I would have said no, but now we're just experiencing that more and more.

00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,900
So I'd say yes.

